  "rationale": "<p>The correct answer is <math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that a mechanical device produces items at a constant rate of <math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math> items per hour. This rate can be written as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 60 items Over 1 hour EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>items</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hour</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. Let <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represent the number of items the mechanical device will produce in <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> hours at the given rate. It follows that <math alttext=\"StartFraction 60 items Over 1 hour EndFraction equals StartFraction x items Over 3 hours EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>items</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hour</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>items</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hours</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>, which can be written as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 60 Over 1 EndFraction equals StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"60 equals StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction\"><mn>60</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"180 equals x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>180</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, at the given rate, the mechanical device will produce <math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn>\n</math> items in <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> hours.</p>\n<p>Alternate approach: It's given that a mechanical device produces items at a constant rate of <math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math> items per hour. At this rate, the mechanical device will produce <math alttext=\"left parenthesis StartFraction 